dashboard.definition:
{
	"title": "Workplace — Single Pane of Glass",
	"inputs": {
		"input_global_trp": {
			"options": {
				"defaultValue": "-30d@d,now",
				"token": "global_time"
			},
			"title": "Time range",
			"type": "input.timerange"
		}
	},
	"defaults": {
		"dataSources": {
			"ds.search": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			},
			"ds.spl2": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			}
		},
		"tokens": {
			"default": {}
		}
	},
	"visualizations": {
		"viz_about_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_about_md": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "# Workplace — Single Pane of Glass\n\n**Audience:** Executive Sponsors, NetOps Leadership, Workplace Services, Cisco Account Team\n\nThis is the executive view aligned to the **Cisco Future-Proof Workplace** strategy paper . It rolls Catalyst Center + Cisco Spaces (Wi-Fi-based, not camera-based) into five Health Tiles. Two tiles are fully wired today; one is a Phase-3 placeholder pending data ingestion. Use this dashboard for monthly business reviews and incident-window readouts. Drill into `NetOps Readiness — Op Florida Ready` for operational detail."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_bmxsRvR0": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_corr": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_annotations",
				"primary": "ds_correlation"
			},
			"description": "When wired and wireless move together = full mobilization. Wireless-only spike = mobile/responder activity. Auth failures climbing post-event = AAR audit work. All signals quiet = a data-source problem, not a quiet day.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": "> annotation | seriesByName('annotation_color')",
				"annotationLabel": "> annotation | seriesByName('label')",
				"annotationX": "> annotation | seriesByName('_time')",
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"lineCurveStyle": "smooth",
				"markerDisplay": "outlined",
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"overlayFields": "AP Health (0-100), Spaces Concurrent Users, Auth Failures",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#649ef5",
					"#049fd9",
					"#4cbf7f",
					"#f7782f",
					"#fa5762"
				],
				"showLegend": true,
				"showOverlayY2Axis": true,
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"y2AxisAbbreviation": "auto",
				"y2AxisTitleText": "AP Health / Spaces / Auth failures",
				"yAxisAbbreviation": "auto",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Wired / Wireless clients",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"lineWidth": 2
			},
			"title": "Cross-source correlation",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_corr_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_corr_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "## Cross-source correlation strip\n\nWired clients, wireless clients, AP health (all DNAC), Spaces presence (post-Apr 17 only), and Windows auth failures on a shared time axis. \n<span style=\"color:#649ef5\">●</span> **Vertical blue markers:** Op Florida Ready exercise — *Day 1 (Apr 13), Day 2 (Apr 14), Day 3 (Apr 15)*. **Reading pattern:** wireless surges + wired stays flat = mobile-driven event. All signals moving together = full operational mobilization. The point: Splunk is the integration fabric tying disparate Cisco + non-Cisco signals into one story."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_footer_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_footer_md": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#a6adb6",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## Phase roadmap *(per Cisco Future-Proof Workplace strategy)*\n\n**Phase 1 — Done:** NetOps Readiness for Op Florida Ready (separate dashboard) + this Workplace SPoG scaffold.\n\n**Phase 2 — In progress:** Tile 4 frictionless-access via badging integration; per-site Spaces hourly heatmap once firehose Apr 13–15 gap is escalated to vendor.\n\n**Phase 3 — Pending:** Tile 3 Energy Intensity (Catalyst 9300X PoE + utility meters); Tile 4 access-control system; Tile 5 OT life-safety / fire-panel integration via BACnet.\n\n**Phase 4 — Visionary:** AI Agents on the data lake — same agentic pattern Cisco deployed for CoreNet in Kuala Lumpur Malaysia. Splunk is the substrate.\n\n*Source: `reference_design/Cisco_FutureProof_Workplace.md`*"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_issues": {
			"context": {
				"viz_issues_Priority_colors": [
					{
						"match": "P1",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "P2",
						"value": "rgba(229,168,35,0.30)"
					},
					{
						"match": "P3",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					},
					{
						"match": "P4",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_issues"
			},
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"columnFormat": {
					"Priority": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"Priority\") | matchValue(viz_issues_Priority_colors)"
					}
				},
				"count": 12,
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"headerBackgroundColor": "#1c2738",
					"headerColor": "#ecf0f5"
				}
			},
			"title": "Top active issues",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_issues_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_issues_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "## Active issues by category\n\nDNAC active issues grouped by category and priority. Top of the list is what's burning right now."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_main_trend": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_annotations",
				"primary": "ds_main_trend"
			},
			"description": "Reading pattern: client load up + AP health steady = elastic capacity. Client load up + AP health dipping = the network is taking the strain. Client load up + issues spiking = something broke under stress.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": "> annotation | seriesByName('annotation_color')",
				"annotationLabel": "> annotation | seriesByName('label')",
				"annotationX": "> annotation | seriesByName('_time')",
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"lineCurveStyle": "smooth",
				"markerDisplay": "outlined",
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"overlayFields": "AP Health (0-100), Active Issues",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#649ef5",
					"#049fd9",
					"#4cbf7f",
					"#fa5762"
				],
				"showLegend": true,
				"showOverlayY2Axis": true,
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"y2AxisAbbreviation": "auto",
				"y2AxisTitleText": "AP Health (0-100) / Active Issues",
				"yAxisAbbreviation": "auto",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Wired / Wireless clients",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"lineWidth": 2
			},
			"title": "Wireless occupancy & quality over time",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_main_trend_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_main_trend_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "## Concurrent endpoints over time — wired vs wireless\n\nDaily concurrent endpoints from DNAC client-health rollup, split by **wired** (desktops, VoIP, kiosks) vs **wireless** (laptops, phones, tablets), overlaid with AP health and active issues. \n<span style=\"color:#649ef5\">●</span> **Vertical blue markers:** Op Florida Ready exercise — *Day 1 (Apr 13), Day 2 (Apr 14), Day 3 (Apr 15)*. **Reading pattern:** wireless surges + wired stays flat = mobile-driven event (responders roaming). Both surge = full-staff mobilization."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_persite": {
			"context": {
				"viz_persite_Status_colors": [
					{
						"match": "At Risk",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Watch",
						"value": "rgba(229,168,35,0.30)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Good",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_persite"
			},
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"columnFormat": {
					"Status": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"Status\") | matchValue(viz_persite_Status_colors)"
					}
				},
				"count": 12,
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"headerBackgroundColor": "#1c2738",
					"headerColor": "#ecf0f5"
				}
			},
			"title": "Site quality leaderboard",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_persite_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_persite_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "## Per-site Network Quality\n\nNQI by site, sorted worst first. Worst sites are where the executive should ask 'why?'"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t1_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_t1_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "**Tile 1 — Occupancy**\n\nTotal concurrent endpoints (wired + wireless) from DNAC client-health rollup. The authoritative count reported by Catalyst Center, not a per-AP estimate."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t1_value": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_t1_occupancy_kpi"
			},
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#049fd9",
				"majorFontSize": 56,
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"shouldUseThousandSeparators": true,
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#649ef5",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23"
			},
			"title": "Total concurrent endpoints (wired + wireless)",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_t2_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_t2_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "**Tile 2 — Network Quality**\n\nComposite Network Quality Index (NQI) blending DNAC AP health and client health, scaled 0–100. Replaces environmental tile (no MT/BMS data ingested)."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t2_value": {
			"context": {
				"majorColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 60,
						"value": "#fa5762"
					},
					{
						"from": 60,
						"to": 80,
						"value": "#f0c243"
					},
					{
						"from": 80,
						"value": "#4cbf7f"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_t2_nqi_kpi"
			},
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "> majorValue | rangeValue(majorColorEditorConfig)",
				"majorFontSize": 60,
				"majorValue": "> primary | seriesByName('NQI') | lastPoint()",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#4cbf7f",
				"unit": "%",
				"unitPosition": "after",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23"
			},
			"title": "Network Quality Index",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_t3_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeDasharray": "4 4",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_t3_placeholder": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "## ⏳\n**Pending data**\nIngestion roadmap:\n- Catalyst 9300X PoE telemetry via DNAC API\n- BACnet / Modbus utility meters\n- Building floor area normalization table\n\nETA: dependent on facilities engagement."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t3_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "**Tile 3 — Energy Intensity** *(Phase 3 — pending)*\n\nReal-time kWh per square foot vs baseline. Requires Catalyst 9300X port-level PoE telemetry + utility meter ingestion. Not yet flowing into Splunk."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t4_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_t4_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "**Tile 4 — Security Posture**\n\nActive P1+P2 DNAC issues plus Windows authentication failures. Frictionless badging deferred to Phase 3 (no access-control system ingested)."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t4_value": {
			"context": {
				"majorColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 10,
						"value": "#4cbf7f"
					},
					{
						"from": 10,
						"to": 30,
						"value": "#f0c243"
					},
					{
						"from": 30,
						"value": "#fa5762"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_t4_security_kpi"
			},
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "> majorValue | rangeValue(majorColorEditorConfig)",
				"majorFontSize": 60,
				"majorValue": "> primary | seriesByName('Active Risks') | lastPoint()",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"shouldUseThousandSeparators": true,
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#fa5762",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23"
			},
			"title": "Active Risks",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_t5_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeWidth": 1,
				"strokeOpacity": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_t5_title": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"markdown": "**Tile 5 — Operational Resilience**\n\nNetwork Readiness Score (NRS) — composite of attainability, retainability, quality, and risk dampening. Same formula as the NetOps Readiness dashboard."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_t5_value": {
			"context": {
				"majorColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 75,
						"value": "#fa5762"
					},
					{
						"from": 75,
						"to": 90,
						"value": "#f0c243"
					},
					{
						"from": 90,
						"value": "#4cbf7f"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_t5_nrs_kpi"
			},
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "> majorValue | rangeValue(majorColorEditorConfig)",
				"majorFontSize": 60,
				"majorValue": "> primary | seriesByName('NRS') | lastPoint()",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#649ef5",
				"unit": "%",
				"unitPosition": "after",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23"
			},
			"title": "Network Readiness Score",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		}
	},
	"dataSources": {
		"ds_annotations": {
			"name": "Shared - Annotations",
			"options": {
				"query": "| noop",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_correlation": {
			"name": "Cross-source correlation - clienthealth wired wireless AP health Spaces auth failures union pattern",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" scoreType=\"ALL\" clientType=\"WIRED\"\n | timechart fixedrange=false latest(clientCount) as \"Wired Clients\" ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" scoreType=\"ALL\" clientType=\"WIRELESS\"\n | timechart fixedrange=false latest(clientCount) as \"Wireless Clients\" ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" OverallHealth=*\n | search DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\" OR DeviceFamily=\"Wireless Controller\"\n | where OverallHealth >= 0\n | timechart avg(OverallHealth) as ap_h_raw\n | eval \"AP Health (0-100)\" = round(ap_h_raw*10, 1)\n | fields - ap_h_raw ]\n [ search `index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\"\n | eval mac=coalesce('devicePresence.device.macAddress','devicePresence.macAddress')\n | where isnotnull(mac) AND mac!=\"\"\n | timechart dc(mac) as \"Spaces Concurrent Users\" ]\n [ search `index_windows` sourcetype=\"WinEventLog:Security\" (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4771)\n | timechart count as \"Auth Failures\" ]\n| stats values(*) as * by _time\n| sort _time\n| table _time, \"Wired Clients\", \"Wireless Clients\", \"AP Health (0-100)\", \"Spaces Concurrent Users\", \"Auth Failures\"",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_issues": {
			"name": "Top active DNAC issues by specific-category and priority",
			"options": {
				"query": "`index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:issue\" IssueStatus=\"active\"\n| stats dc(IssueID) as Issues, latest(_time) as last_seen by IssueSpecificCategory, IssuePriority\n| eval \"Last seen\" = strftime(last_seen, \"%a %m/%d %H:%M\")\n| sort -Issues\n| rename IssueSpecificCategory as Category, IssuePriority as Priority\n| fields - last_seen\n| table Category Priority Issues \"Last seen\"",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_main_trend": {
			"name": "Main trend - wired wireless from clienthealth AP health issues daily union pattern",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" scoreType=\"ALL\" clientType=\"WIRED\"\n | timechart fixedrange=false latest(clientCount) as \"Wired Clients\" ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" scoreType=\"ALL\" clientType=\"WIRELESS\"\n | timechart fixedrange=false latest(clientCount) as \"Wireless Clients\" ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" OverallHealth=*\n | search DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\" OR DeviceFamily=\"Wireless Controller\"\n | where OverallHealth >= 0\n | timechart avg(OverallHealth) as ap_h_raw\n | eval \"AP Health (0-100)\" = round(ap_h_raw*10, 1)\n | fields - ap_h_raw ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:issue\" IssueStatus=\"active\"\n | timechart dc(IssueID) as \"Active Issues\" ]\n| stats values(*) as * by _time\n| sort _time\n| table _time, \"Wired Clients\", \"Wireless Clients\", \"AP Health (0-100)\", \"Active Issues\"",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_persite": {
			"name": "Per-site Network Quality leaderboard",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\"\n | search DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\" OR DeviceFamily=\"Wireless Controller\"\n | eval site=coalesce(Site, Location)\n | where isnotnull(site) AND trim(site)!=\"\" AND lower(site)!=\"null\" AND NOT match(site, \"(?i)(^|/)null(/|$)\")\n | stats latest(Reachability) as reach, latest(OverallHealth) as oh by DeviceName, site\n | eval is_reach=if(upper(reach)=\"REACHABLE\", 1, 0)\n | eval ap_ok=case(isnull(oh), null(), oh<0, null(), oh>=7, 1, 1=1, 0)\n | stats avg(is_reach) as ap_reach, avg(ap_ok) as ap_health_ok, count as ap_n by site ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\" siteHierarchy=*\n | eval cl_health = 'health.overallScore', site = siteHierarchy\n | where isnotnull(site) AND trim(site)!=\"\" AND lower(site)!=\"null\" AND NOT match(site, \"(?i)(^|/)null(/|$)\")\n | stats avg(cl_health) as health_avg, count as cl_n by site\n | eval health100=coalesce(health_avg,8)*10 ]\n| stats values(ap_reach) as ap_reach, values(ap_health_ok) as ap_ok,\n values(health100) as h100, values(ap_n) as ap_n, values(cl_n) as cl_n by site\n| where (isnotnull(ap_n) AND ap_n>0) OR (isnotnull(cl_n) AND cl_n>0)\n| eval ap_reach=coalesce(ap_reach,1), ap_ok=coalesce(ap_ok,1), h100=coalesce(h100,80)\n| eval NQI = round((ap_ok*100)*0.6 + h100*0.4, 1)\n| eval Status = case(NQI>=85, \"Good\", NQI>=70, \"Watch\", 1=1, \"At Risk\")\n| eval site_short=replace(site, \"^Global/Florida/\", \"\")\n| sort + NQI\n| rename site_short as Site, ap_n as APs, cl_n as Clients\n| table Site NQI Status APs Clients",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_t1_occupancy_kpi": {
			"name": "Tile 1 - total concurrent endpoints wired wireless via clienthealth",
			"options": {
				"query": "`index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" scoreType=\"ALL\" (clientType=\"WIRED\" OR clientType=\"WIRELESS\")\n| timechart fixedrange=false latest(clientCount) by clientType\n| addtotals fieldname=\"Total Endpoints\"\n| fields _time, \"Total Endpoints\"",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_t2_nqi_kpi": {
			"name": "Tile 2 - Network Quality Index with sparkline",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" OverallHealth=*\n | search DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\" OR DeviceFamily=\"Wireless Controller\"\n | where OverallHealth >= 0\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats avg(OverallHealth) as ap_health by _time\n | eval ap100 = ap_health*10 ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\"\n | eval cs = 'health.overallScore'\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats avg(cs) as cl_health by _time\n | eval cl100 = cl_health*10 ]\n| stats values(ap100) as ap100, values(cl100) as cl100 by _time\n| eval NQI = round(coalesce(ap100,80)*0.6 + coalesce(cl100,80)*0.4, 1)\n| timechart span=1d max(NQI) as NQI",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_t4_security_kpi": {
			"name": "Tile 4 - active P1 P2 risks plus auth failures with sparkline",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:issue\" IssueStatus=\"active\" (IssuePriority=\"P1\" OR IssuePriority=\"P2\")\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats dc(IssueID) as dnac_risk by _time ]\n [ search `index_windows` sourcetype=\"WinEventLog:Security\" (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4771)\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats count as auth_fail by _time ]\n| stats values(dnac_risk) as dnac_risk, values(auth_fail) as auth_fail by _time\n| eval dnac_risk=coalesce(dnac_risk,0), auth_fail=coalesce(auth_fail,0)\n| eval auth_fail_norm = if(auth_fail>0, ceil(auth_fail/100), 0)\n| eval risks = dnac_risk + auth_fail_norm\n| timechart span=1d max(risks) as \"Active Risks\"",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		},
		"ds_t5_nrs_kpi": {
			"name": "Tile 5 - NRS daily with sparkline",
			"options": {
				"query": "| union\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" OverallHealth=*\n | search DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\" OR DeviceFamily=\"Wireless Controller\"\n | where OverallHealth >= 0\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats latest(Reachability) as reach, latest(OverallHealth) as oh by _time, DeviceName\n | eval is_reach=if(upper(reach)=\"REACHABLE\", 1, 0), ap_ok=if(oh>=`nrs_th_ap_health`, 1, 0)\n | stats avg(is_reach) as ap_reach, avg(ap_ok) as ap_health_ok, count as ap_n by _time ]\n [ search `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\"\n | eval cl_health = 'health.overallScore'\n | bin _time span=1d \n | stats avg(cl_health) as health_avg, count(eval(cl_health>=`nrs_th_cl_health`)) as ok_n, count as cl_n by _time\n | eval cl_ok=if(cl_n>0, ok_n/cl_n, null()), health100=coalesce(health_avg,8)*10 ]\n| stats values(ap_reach) as ap_reach, values(ap_health_ok) as ap_ok,\n values(cl_ok) as cl_ok, values(health100) as h100,\n values(ap_n) as ap_n, values(cl_n) as cl_n by _time\n| where isnotnull(ap_n) AND ap_n>0\n| eval ap_reach=coalesce(ap_reach,1), ap_ok=coalesce(ap_ok,1),\n cl_ok=coalesce(cl_ok,1), h100=coalesce(h100,80)\n| eval A=ap_reach*100, R=(ap_ok*0.5 + cl_ok*0.5)*100, Q=h100\n| eval NRS=A*`nrs_w_nrs_a` + R*`nrs_w_nrs_r` + Q*`nrs_w_nrs_q`\n| timechart span=1d max(eval(round(NRS, 2))) as NRS",
				"queryParameters": {
					"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
					"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
				}
			},
			"type": "ds.search"
		}
	},
